      "notes": "OBJ_FWIP_ID -> FWIP (22 params). FWIP is empty on this device: DM names are the OBJ names, unverified. Stock posts Protocol 0-4 and FilterTarget 0/1 as numbers directly (labels 'refuse'/'Permit'); note the firmware has a different protocol table (TCP 0, UDP 1, ICMP 2, ANY 3) elsewhere, so check one stored rule before trusting codes 2-4. Stock writes -1 to all ports for ICMP/Any and for empty ports, '' for empty IPs. Ingress/egress options are the runtime OBJ_WANLAN_ID list (WAN connections and LAN bridges); a runtime option source would help. Name: 1-32 chars, codes 1-255 (checkGenStringForASC). Stock also validates start <= end for IP and port ranges (cross-field, not expressible here). Stock applies through OBJ_* set_inst, which notifies the firewall module at once. A raw `sidbg DB set` + save is expected to need a reboot (or a firewall reload) to take effect; unverified. UI-text notes moved here: [INCViewName]: Interface identity such as a WAN connection or LAN view name; empty = any."
