      "notes": "OBJ_FWSC_ID -> FWSC (DM names verified on the device; the stock param list omits Name). The DM really is spelled 'Servise'. Services are a bitmask (stock hexVal 1/2/4/8/16/32 = HTTP/FTP/SSH/TELNET/HTTPS/SNMP); a checkbox-group field type would render it better. IPMode: stock writes 1 for IPv4 and 2 for IPv6. FWBase IsWanSrvCntl/SrvCntlTarget/DefaultPolicy are not on the stock page (the param list carries them through untouched); SrvCntlTarget code meaning assumed Discard 0/Permit 1. A Discard rule on a LAN ingress for HTTP or Telnet locks the admin out of this UI and of telnet - hence commit-confirm. 'Modify remote access port' links to sec-service-ports. Stock applies through OBJ_* set_inst, which notifies the firewall module at once. A raw `sidbg DB set` + save is expected to need a reboot (or a firewall reload) to take effect; unverified. UI-text notes moved here: [INCViewName]: IGD.WANIF = any WAN; otherwise a LAN bridge identity. Empty = any. | [MinSrcIp]: 0.0.0.0 = any (stock writes 0.0.0.0 for IPv6 rules). | [Prefix]: Stock writes :: for IPv4 rules. | [Servise]: Bitmask: HTTP 1, FTP 2, SSH 4, Telnet 8, HTTPS 16, SNMP 32. IPv6 rules only use HTTP and HTTPS."
